(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[12 1 "// Interp is an interpreter (PyInterpreterState): its builtins, its modules (sys.modules), its standard"] [13 1 "// streams and its recursion limit."] [22 1 "// NewInterp is a fresh interpreter writing to stdout and stderr."] [32 1 "// startXOptions are the -X options of the command line (queue 220): bin/pyi python passes them in PYI_XOPTIONS, one"] [33 1 "// per line, NAME or NAME=VALUE; read once and removed from the environment (a child of the program does not inherit"] [34 1 "// them, as -X is not inherited)."] [54 1 "// startEnv is os.Getenv of a PYTHON* variable at start: \"\" under -E or -I (bin/pyi python's PYI_IGNORE_ENV, read once"] [55 1 "// and removed from the environment as PYI_XOPTIONS is)."] [72 2 "// atStartHooks run before the main module (Py_InitializeMain's late steps: queue 220, faulthandler's enable for"] [73 2 "// -X faulthandler and PYTHONFAULTHANDLER); an error is printed and the run's status is 1"] [77 1 "// cModeFile is the file bin/pyi python writes -c's code into (queue 220): run as CPython runs -c, its code's file"] [78 1 "// \"<string>\", no __file__, sys.path[0] \"\"."] [81 1 "// ExecModule runs a module's code object as the module name (its namespace's __name__), returning"] [82 1 "// the module, or the uncaught exception."] [87 1 "// PrintException writes an uncaught exception as CPython's default excepthook does"] [88 1 "// (Lib/traceback.py's format): the chain first (__cause__, else __context__ unless suppressed), each"] [89 1 "// with its traceback (the file, line and function, and the source line when the file reads) and"] [90 1 "// \"Type: text\", a SyntaxError's location and caret, the notes. Carets under expressions are not"] [91 1 "// printed (PY5b: a recorded difference)."] [92 1 "//"] [93 1 "// The text goes to sys.stderr (PyErr_Display's file): the process's standard error while sys.stderr is"] [94 1 "// the one it started with, else the text is written by sys.stderr.write and